{"parentUuid":"47d51bfc-4a9c-4e67-b450-51183229fe0a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGUWNC4aZgtFKEZnV8z1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm digging into finding 3 about draft loss on sidebar clicks — since the outside-click protection was removed, navigation clicks no longer get blocked while editing a note. I want to check how ExpandedItemOverlay tracks editing state and whether App could use a ref or flag set by the overlay to guard navigation handlers like selectSpace, settings, or clearToDefaultView from firing mid-edit.\n\nI'm weighing options: autosave on unmount preserves the user's edit but changes the cancel semantics, while caching the draft by item id in something like noteBodyCacheRef lets it persist and restore cleanly. I want to trace back through the git history to see exactly what outside-click protection existed in the main version's overlay before it was removed.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1304,"cache_read_input_tokens":180573,"output_tokens":602,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":314},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1304,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":602,"cache_read_input_tokens":180573,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1304,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1304},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":6080,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGUWMtDcdq72VQjEEPW9","requestRef":"f36a93f1-fe1c-4b08-a3d6-75ecffce8c3f","requestedModel":"claude-opus-5-5","type":"a