{"type":"api-request-blob","sessionId":"fad76192-bf94-45bb-9f1a-d29cda113db7","hash":"b0210b6ad2c7c9a528402e376476278f365d8c94ef61f65c696ebc997e5d87ed","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The persist functions themselves don't manage capturing state, that's handled by the capture wrappers. So saveFromAddMenu needs to set isCapturing around the save, plus use a ref to prevent a synchronous double-Enter before the rerender happens.\n\n","signature":""},{"type":"text","text":"The `persist*` functions never set `isCapturing`, so the menu's \"Saving…\" state never turns on. I'll wrap the save in that flag, with a ref guarding against a second Enter before the re-render."},{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SdYDeMiKHS28vBKHADgHwS","name":"Edit","input":{"file_path":"C:\\Users\\chris\\.t3\\worktrees\\inkling\\t3-47ff5304\\src\\App.tsx","old_string":"  async function saveFromAddMenu(save: () => Promise<unknown>) {\n    setCaptureError(null);\n    try {\n      await save();\n      setIsAdding(false);\n      setCaptureMode(null);\n      return true;\n    } catch (error) {\n      setCaptureError(error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error));\n      return false;\n    }\n  }","new_string":"  // A second Enter can land before the saving state re-renders, so a ref\n  // keeps one save at a time.\n  const addMenuSavingRef = useRef(false);\n  async function saveFromAddMenu(save: () => Promise<unknown>) {\n    if (addMenuSavingRef.current) return false;\n    addMenuSavingRef.current = true;\n    setCaptureError(null);\n    setIsCapturing(true);\n    try {\n      await save();\n      setIsAdding(false);\n      setCaptureMode(null);\n      return true;\n    } catch (error) {\n      setCaptureError(error instanceof Error ? error.message : String(error));\n      return false;\n    } finally {\n      addMenuSavingRef.current = false;\n      setIsCapturing(false);\n    }\n  }"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}]}}
