{"parentUuid":"7e95df0c-fd91-47c4-953c-f49577930511","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgGUaBtp5SsZ3RfCWN5UR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"I'm wondering if the kind restriction exists to avoid clobbering detail-loaded fields like articleHtml or noteBody, since spreading refreshed data over current won't remove fields unless they're explicitly set undefined—and storedItemToLibraryItem does set keys like palette explicitly, which could overwrite unintended fields. For images specifically, I need to figure out which fields actually matter, like image, palette, dimensions, and processing state.\n\nImages sometimes lack sourceUrl entirely since they're local files, so the `!current?.sourceUrl` condition unintentionally excludes them—I should change the gate to allow Image kind regardless of sourceUrl and add palette to the changed check. I also want to check whether patchChangedItems properly syncs selection state.\n\n","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1513,"cache_read_input_tokens":191110,"output_tokens":450,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":323},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1513,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":191110,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1513,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1513},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"thinkingDurationMs":5512,"thinkingDisplay":"summarized","apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CgGUaBTm3JAvEJZZFcNrK","requestRef":"759f1ef7-1f53-4e27-b74f-9120bb3d03c1","requestedModel":